  "manchester-c398-p133": {
    "title": "水家苗（題字待核）",
    "title_en": "水家苗（題字待核） — provisional Manchester source reading",
    "page_kind": "caption",
    "status": "image_checked_draft",
    "ocr_raw": "水家苗在荔波郡地方，自雍正十年由粵西而轉於黔之都匀府。男喜漁獵，女善紡織。有林家布之名，穿短衣桶裙，四圍均以花布縫之。每歲首男女成群連袂歌舞，相悅，女負之去，遂婚娶。",
    "transcription": "水家苗在荔波郡地方，自雍正十年由粵西而轉於黔之都匀府。男喜漁獵，女善紡織。有林家布之名，穿短衣桶裙，四圍均以花布縫之。每歲首男女成群連袂歌舞，相悅，女負之去，遂婚娶。",
    "translation": "The Shuijia Miao [heading to be verified] live around Libo. In the tenth year of Yongzheng, their territory was transferred from western Guangdong/Guangxi to Duyun Prefecture in Guizhou. Men enjoy fishing and hunting, while women are skilled at spinning and weaving. Their cloth is known as “Linjia cloth.” They wear short garments and tubular skirts, edged all around with flower-patterned cloth. At the beginning of each year, men and women form groups, join hands, sing, and dance. When they take a liking to someone, a woman carries [or takes] that person away [the object of the verb is uncertain], and marriage follows.",
    "translation_status": "ai_draft",
    "transcription_scope": "full_page_visual_pass_provisional_with_uncertain_characters",
    "text_completeness": "provisional_full_or_near_full",
    "english_completeness": "full_relative_to_chinese_draft",
    "translation_scope": "Full English rendering of current provisional Chinese transcript in source order; [unreadable] denotes unresolved source reading. Not a human-certified edition.",
    "ocr_engine": "AI-assisted visual manuscript reading, not automated OCR",
    "source_review": "User-uploaded Manchester Chinese Crawford 398 IIIF canvas 133 (source checked 2026-11-22)",
    "notes": "依上傳曼徹斯特本原圖按竪排自右向左試錄；存疑字保留□；非人工定稿，歷史族稱反映原編繪者立場。 英文為試譯性概述，並非逐字對譯。",
    "english_kind": "source_aligned_translation_draft",
    "prior_english_summary_20261122": "The source locates the Shuijia Miao in Libo and refers to an administrative transfer from western Guangdong/Guangxi into Duyun during the Yongzheng reign. Men are said to fish and hunt, women to weave, including a cloth called Linjia fabric. Festive dancing and partner selection lead to marriage. The first character and historical geography need checking against the scan.",
    "translation_full_draft_20261122": true
  },
