    "page_kind": "caption",
    "status": "image_checked_draft",
    "ocr_raw": "白兒子，威寧州及滇者有之。俱有家族，男多漢人風業，趕□牛貿易，女猶沿苗俗。原是漢人招贅苗女為家室，其俗相仍，故名白兒子。",
    "transcription": "白兒子，威寧州及滇者有之。俱有家族，男多漢人風業，趕□牛貿易，女猶沿苗俗。原是漢人招贅苗女為家室，其俗相仍，故名白兒子。",
    "translation": "The Bai'erzi live in Weining Prefecture and in Yunnan. They all have family lineages. Men often follow Han occupations and customs, driving [unreadable] cattle for trade; women still maintain Miao customs. According to the account, Han men originally married into Miao women's families and established households there. The practice persisted, hence the name Bai'erzi.",
    "translation_status": "ai_draft",
