    "text_completeness": "provisional_full_or_near_full",
    "english_completeness": "full_relative_to_chinese_draft",
    "translation_scope": "Full English rendering of current provisional Chinese transcript in source order; [unreadable] denotes unresolved source reading. Not a human-certified edition.",
    "ocr_engine": "AI-assisted visual reading from page image; not automated OCR",
    "source_review": "Manchester Chinese Crawford 398, user-supplied IIIF canvas 145; checked 2026-11-22",
    "notes": "已依原頁右至左欄次做圖像校讀初稿；難辨字作□，未經人工學術校訂。 英文為試譯性概述，並非逐字對譯。",
    "english_kind": "source_aligned_translation_draft",
    "prior_english_summary_20261122": "The Bai Erzi are described in Weining and Yunnan. Men reportedly engage in trade and follow Han customs, while women retain Miao customs. The compiler explains their name through Han men joining Miao women's households through uxorilocal marriage. One trade-related character remains uncertain.",
